2. Manual (Authored) Quest-Making Capabilities
Manual quests are authored in public/data/campaigns/<campaign_id>/quests.json (or via the in-app Campaign Editor) and validated by QuestSchema (src/types/quests.types.ts).
A. Quest & Objective Schema (QuestSchema)
Logical Combinators (logicalOperator: 'AND' | 'OR'):
'AND' (default): All objectives in the quest must reach requiredAmount.
'OR': Completing any single objective in the list satisfies the quest (enabling branching "kill the warlord OR talk/bribe your way past" resolutions).
5 Objective Types (QuestObjectiveSchema):
'kill' — Target an entity template ID (targetId: "goblin", requiredAmount: 3).
'talk' — Speak to an NPC template ID (targetId: "scout", requiredAmount: 1).
'gather' — Acquire an item ID (targetId: "health_potion", requiredAmount: 2).
'explore' — Reach/discover a target area or location.
'interact' — Use a specific world prop/feature (altar, lever, chest).
Completion Modes (autoComplete: boolean):
autoComplete: true: The moment the objective threshold is met, completeQuest() fires immediately in the field.
autoComplete: false: Meeting the objectives keeps the quest 'active' until an NPC dialogue option or world trigger explicitly fires the complete_quest consequence (classic CRPG "return to quest-giver" turn-in).
Visibility (isHidden?: boolean): Supports hidden/secret tracking quests that don't clutter the journal UI.
Wiki-Link Hypertext: Titles, descriptions, and objective strings support [Goblin](entity:goblin) syntax, which quest.ui.ts parses into interactive hoverable tooltip links.
B. Runtime O(1) Event Routing (QuestLogComponent)
Stored on the player entity in QuestLogComponent:
quests: Record<string, { status: 'active' | 'completed' | 'failed', objectiveProgress: Record<string, number> }>
activeTriggers: Record<string, ReadonlyArray<{ questId: string; objectiveId: string }>>
Whenever a quest is granted or completed, rebuildQuestTriggers() indexes all active objectives by "${obj.type}:${obj.targetId}" (e.g., "kill:goblin"). When processQuestEvent(state, 'kill', 'goblin', 1) runs, it performs an O(1) lookup instead of scanning every quest in the campaign.
C. Intersections with Triggers & Dialogues
Trigger System (src/systems/trigger.system.ts & src/systems/trigger/quest.ts):
Events: quest.system.ts emits GameEventType.QuestStageChanged (whenever an objective increments) and GameEventType.QuestCompleted.
Conditions: Triggers and Dialogue options can gate on quest_status (target: questId, operator: '==' | '>=' | '<=', where 0 = active, 1 = completed, 2 = failed, -1 = not started).
Consequences: Any dialogue option or world trigger can execute grant_quest or complete_quest.
Editor & Validator Tooling:
quest.validator.ts verifies that 'kill' objectives reference valid entity IDs and 'gather' objectives reference valid item IDs that actually exist in the loot table.
narrative_fuzzer.ts runs Monte Carlo walk simulations across dialogue trees and triggers to catch deadlocks or unreachable quest states.
3. Procedural & Emergent Quest-Making Capabilities
The engine has a second registry inside GameState: state.dynamicQuests: Record<string, Quest>, alongside getQuestDef(state, questId) which seamlessly resolves both static (state.campaign.quests[id]) and procedural (state.dynamicQuests[id]) quests.
Currently, procedural quests and emergent objectives come from three sources:
Template-Driven Procedural Bounties (src/systems/procedural-quest.system.ts):
Reads quest_templates.json (QuestTemplateSchema), which defines titleTemplate, descriptionTemplate, objectiveType, targetTags, targetFactions, amountRange: [min, max], and rewardXpMultiplier.
generateProceduralQuest(state, templateId) uses the deterministic rng to pick a matching entity template, roll a count in [min, max], format wiki-linked strings, compute scaled XP, and register dyn_<templateId>_<nextQuestId> into state.dynamicQuests.
Economy-Driven Merchant Supply Runs (src/systems/shop.system.ts):
When a merchant's ShopComponent.inventory is depleted, restockShop() has a 50% chance to procedurally generate a dyn_restock_<shopEntityId>_<nextQuestId> 'gather' quest for 1–3x items matching the merchant's buyTags, registering it into state.dynamicQuests.
Emergent Villain Schemes & Investigation Loop (scheme.system.ts + investigation.system.ts + gossip.system.ts):
Mastermind Schemes: Villains compile multi-phase schemes (SchemeRecipe + PhaseBlocks) that recruit NPC minions via MICE personality profiling (AgreementComponent) and mutate dungeon areas (SchemeMutatedArea).
Clue Drops: Killing a minion with an AgreementComponent triggers the has_agreement condition -> spawn_clue consequence (src/systems/trigger/quest.ts), dropping a physical scroll with a ClueComponent implicating the mastermind.
Investigation Board & Stall Detector: Picking up clues fires ClueDiscoveredEvent, adding secrets/suspects to the player's MemoryComponent.knowledge and state.investigation. If the player goes too many turns (INVESTIGATION_STALL_THRESHOLD) without finding a clue, investigation.system.ts emits GameEventType.InvestigationStalled, which the Trigger/Drama Director can use to inject a lead or ambush.
4. Honest Audit: Current Gaps & Unfinished Wiring
While the foundational architecture (schemas, O(1) trigger map, dual static/dynamic registries, trigger/dialogue hooks, investigation board) is clean and in place, several critical pieces are currently half-wired or stubbed:
Only 2 of the 5 Objective Types Are Emitted in Gameplay:
'kill' is emitted in src/systems/death.system.ts:142.
'talk' is emitted in src/systems/dialogue.system.ts:38.
'gather', 'explore', and 'interact' are never called via processQuestEvent()! Picking up an item, entering an area, or interacting with a prop does not currently notify quest.system.ts.
Only 'xp' Rewards Are Paid Out on Completion:
QuestRewardSchema supports 4 reward types: 'xp', 'item', 'standing' (faction reputation), and 'event'.
However, in src/systems/quest.system.ts:54–61, completeQuest() only processes reward.type === 'xp' and has a literal comment: // Future: handle item/standing rewards here. (Even tutorial_quest in default/quests.json defines an 'item' reward of 2 health potions that currently gets ignored!)
Procedural Quests Are Generated, But Not Granted/Exposed via Notice Boards or NPCs:
generateProceduralQuest() in src/systems/procedural-quest.system.ts has zero callers in src/.
restockShop() puts dyn_restock_* quests into state.dynamicQuests, but nothing grants them to the player's QuestLogComponent or displays available dynamic contracts on a Notice Board / Merchant dialogue node.
In procedural-quest.system.ts:24–34, if a template specifies targetTags (like "bounty_kill" in default/quest_templates.json which has targetTags: ["monster"]), the filter unconditionally returns false unless targetFactions is also set, because entity tag filtering wasn't finished there.
Single-Stage Flat Objectives vs. Multi-Stage CRPG Quests:
Right now, a Quest is a single flat list of objectives (AND/OR). To do a multi-stage quest ("1. Investigate the crypt -> 2. Confront the necromancer OR take his bribe -> 3. Report back to the Mayor"), you currently have to chain separate Quest IDs via triggers (Quest A completes -> grants Quest B) rather than advancing stages/branches inside a single journal entry.
No Cartridge / D&D 3.5e Skill & Ability Integration in Quests/Dialogues Yet:
Classic CRPG quests heavily feature skill/ability checks in dialogues and interactions ([Diplomacy DC 15], [Search DC 12], [Knowledge (Religion) DC 15], [STR 14]), as well as XP awards scaled by Encounter Level / CR or party level. Currently, dialogue/trigger conditions check Console-level MemoryComponent facts, faction standing, and personality, but don't yet have a clean Tier 1 -> Tier 2 hook for ruleset skill/ability checks.
